# House sparrow

The house sparrow is the small brown-and-grey sparrow that follows human
settlement almost everywhere on earth. It builds a bulky, domed nest of dry
grass and straw inside a hole in a wall, under a roof tile or in a nest box,
lining the chamber with feathers. Where no cavity is available it will build a
free-standing nest of grass in a tree, which is unusual for the family. It feeds
mainly on seed and scraps, and the young are raised largely on insects. See
[[passeridae]].
